sorders. Her active involvement in the hospital's operations and her collaboration with Dr. Santamaría Sandi highlight the strong leadership within the endocrinology department, which is crucial for advancing patient outcomes. [Data: Entities (3646); Relationships (12077)]\n\n## The significance of the Beyond Ageing Project\n\nThe Beyond Ageing Project is a randomized controlled trial aimed at preventing cognitive decline in older adults through supplementation of folic acid and vitamin B-12. This project represents a significant research initiative that could have far-reaching implications for public health, particularly in addressing age-related cognitive decline. The involvement of Hospital Universitario Cruces in this project underscores its commitment to advancing medical research and improving health outcomes for older populations. [Data: Entities (7902); Relationships (12093)]\n\n## Collaborative research efforts in endocrinology\n\nThe relationships among the entities in this community indicate a strong collaborative effort in the field of endocrinology. Dr. Santamaría Sandi's membership in the Sociedad Española de Endocrinología y Nutrición and his leadership at Hospital Universitario Cruces facilitate a network of professionals dedicated to advancing research and clinical practices. This collaboration is vital for addressing the challenges in endocrinology and nutrition, ultimately benefiting patient care and treatment outcomes. [Data: Relationships (6182, 12092)]", "# Fco. Javier Santamaría Sandi and the Basque Medical Community\n\nThis community centers around Fco. Javier Santamaría Sandi, a prominent endocrinologist affiliated with the Hospital Universitario Cruces and the Universidad del País Vasco. His relationships with various medical and educational institutions highlight his influence in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition in the Basque Country.\n\n## Fco. Javier Santamaría Sandi's professional prominence\n\nFco. Javier Santamaría Sandi is a