 is centered around the Sociedad Española de Endocrinología y Nutrición (SEEN), which plays a pivotal role in the research, education, and treatment of endocrine and nutritional disorders in Spain. Key entities include various authors and contributors to the Manual de Endocrinología y Nutrición, as well as the Dysphagia Therapy app, which supports medical professionals in managing swallowing disorders.\n\n## Central Role of Sociedad Española de Endocrinología y Nutrición\n\nThe Sociedad Española de Endocrinología y Nutrición (SEEN) is a key entity in this community, dedicated to advancing the fields of endocrinology and nutrition in Spain. SEEN is involved in research, education, and the dissemination of guidelines and resources, making it a vital institution for healthcare professionals. Its commitment to addressing endocrine and nutritional disorders is reflected in its various publications, including the Manual de Endocrinología y Nutrición, which serves as a comprehensive resource for practitioners. The organization's influence extends to collaborations with other entities, such as Alianza másnutridos, to tackle malnutrition and related issues [Data: Entities (1286); Relationships (6224)].\n\n## Dysphagia Therapy App's Contribution\n\nThe Dysphagia Therapy app is designed to assist medical professionals in evaluating and managing swallowing disorders, highlighting the community's focus on practical tools for healthcare. This mobile application is specifically tailored to support rehabilitation options for patients with dysphagia, showcasing the integration of technology in medical practice. The app's development underlines the community's commitment to enhancing patient care through innovative solutions, which is crucial for improving health outcomes in individuals with swallowing difficulties [Data: Entities (1287); Relationships (320)].\n\n## Educational Resources and Publications\n\nThe community is characterized by its extensive educational resources, includ